"} {"question" "q-119309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2y-{y}^{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-119309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,1),(1,1)$ and $(1,2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,1)}=2(1)-{1}^{2}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,1)}=2(1)-{1}^{2}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,2)}=2(2)-{2}^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/21828e2eb3d107ea12e90d715de9a3c1350e6fd95f03b321be7ab81a8824b065.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-119309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "387d3f02a5663f54b107e68bcfa7987176dc6e06a6500c05ca757abc31eea180"} {"question" "q-119309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/C