ribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-119305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-1,1),(1,1)$ and $(1,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,1)}=-{1}^{2}=-1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,1)}=-{1}^{2}=-1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,-1)}=-(-1)^{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/bb078d2e632ef5cc29f0e03903a148c8caf0ded552ab9b2604c5b3ecf586d0c4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-119305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "387d3f02a5663f54b107e68bcfa7987176dc6e06a6500c05ca757abc31eea180"} {"question" "q-119305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-captu