 $y=-2,$ the slope field has a positive slope\n- At every point along the line $y=-1,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope field has a negative slope" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,-2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-2)}=-2+1=-1<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is negative for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is equal to $-1$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,-1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-1)}=-1+1=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-1)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}=1+1=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is equal to $2$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/caa69f6116eba6462c4fe18f2e535d83db350f0797cf1fcd895ac6df9a4d6fd7.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "387d3f02a5663f54b107e68bcfa7987176dc6e06a6500c05ca757abc31eea180"} {"question" "q-97288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of those listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point along the line $y=-2,$ the slope field has a negative slope\n- At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope field has a positive slope" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,-2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-2)}=(-2)^{2}=4>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is equal to $4$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,0)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,0)}=(0)^{2}=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,0)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}=(1)^{2}=1>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,1)$ is equal to $1$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/0c6e2e486ae770bc99ef9fe41f02d224de65119ade910d303ad3f57f12e8d84b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "387d3f02a5663f54b107e68bcfa7987176dc6e06a6500c05ca757abc31eea180"} {"question" "q-97291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-97291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd015bcdce88748b0ab869510589ee853438ce853467733016e8d8bfa70131a7"} {"question" "q-119294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-cap